# ============================================================
# SUPABASE DIRECT USAGE
# ============================================================

Do NOT migrate these to TanStack Query — leave them as-is:
- src/lib/supabase.ts — client initialization only
- src/app/contexts/AuthContext.tsx — Supabase auth state
- src/app/pages/app/SafetyPlan.tsx — direct PostgREST query
- Storage uploads in ProfileSetup, UserProfile, AccountSettings
- Realtime subscription in NotificationsContext

NotificationsContext Realtime rule:
The Supabase channel subscription MUST have cleanup:
  const channel = supabase
    .channel(`notifications:${user.id}`)
    .on('postgres_changes', { ... }, handleNewNotification)
    .subscribe((status) => {
      if (status === 'CHANNEL_ERROR') 
        console.warn('Notification channel error')
    })
  return () => { supabase.removeChannel(channel) }

# ============================================================
# PERFORMANCE RULES
# ============================================================

- Never import Three.js outside of ActiveSession-related files
- Always use dynamic import() for jspdf inside async functions:
  const { jsPDF } = await import('jspdf')
- Use React.memo() on components that receive stable props 
  and are rendered in lists or dashboards
- Use useCallback() for functions passed as props to 
  memoized children
- Use useMemo() for expensive calculations that depend on data
- Never do data transformation inside JSX — do it above the return
- Virtualize lists over 50 items using react-window if performance 
  is an issue
- Images must have explicit width and height to avoid layout shift
- Avoid anonymous functions in JSX event handlers on hot paths:
  WRONG:  onClick={() => handleDelete(id)}
  RIGHT:  const handleDeleteClick = useCallback(() => handleDelete(id), [id])

# ============================================================
# ERROR HANDLING
# ============================================================

- Always handle loading and error states from useQuery
- Use toast.error() from sonner for user-facing errors
- Never show raw error objects or stack traces to users
- Log errors to console in development only
- Use error boundaries for critical sections (already in App.tsx)
- For mutations, always handle onError:
  useMutation({
    mutationFn: ...,
    onSuccess: () => toast.success('Saved successfully'),
    onError: (error) => toast.error('Something went wrong'),
  })

# ============================================================
# TYPESCRIPT RULES
# ============================================================

- Strict mode is enabled — never disable it
- No implicit any — always type function parameters
- Prefer interface over type for object shapes
- Use type for unions, intersections, and utility types
- Always type API response data — check src/lib/api.ts for 
  existing response types
- Avoid type assertions (as Type) unless absolutely necessary
- Use optional chaining (?.) and nullish coalescing (??) 
  instead of && checks for nullable values

# ============================================================
# BACKEND RULES (apps/api)
# ============================================================

- Never change Fastify route signatures or prefixes
- Never change Prisma schema without explicit instruction
- Never remove auth middleware (authenticate, authorize)
- All Prisma findMany must have take (pagination limit)
- All Prisma queries should use select to avoid fetching 
  unused columns — never select all implicitly
- Use Prisma transactions for multi-table writes
- Always validate input with Zod schemas on routes
- Never expose internal error details in API responses
- Log errors with request.log.error() not console.error()

# ============================================================
# GIT AND FILE RULES
# ============================================================

- Never commit .env files
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or URLs
- Use environment variables via import.meta.env.VITE_* in web
- Use process.env.* in api and realtime
- Always use pnpm — never npm or yarn
- Run pnpm build after vite.config.ts changes to verify
- If a file hash is unchanged after an edit, 
  the file was not saved — try the edit again
- Show full file contents after any change so I can verify

# ============================================================
# WHAT TO ALWAYS DO
# ============================================================

- Show the full updated file after every change
- Confirm which files were modified
- Ask before installing any new package
- Ask before changing any shared component used in many places
- Ask before changing routing or auth logic
- Prefer editing existing patterns over introducing new ones
- When in doubt about the right approach, ask

# ============================================================
# WHAT TO NEVER DO
# ============================================================

- Never use npm or yarn (pnpm only)
- Never remove existing error handling or toast notifications
- Never change component names or export signatures
- Never change JSX layout or Tailwind classes unless asked
- Never add MUI components — use Radix + Tailwind instead
- Never fetch data inside a modal or dialog component
- Never use localStorage to cache server data
- Never hardcode user IDs, org IDs, or environment URLs
- Never skip TypeScript